==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|tomar}}, of {{unk|pt|title=unknown}} origin. Possibly derived from {{cog|la|autumo|autumāre|to reckon; to affirm}}<ref>Yakov Malkiel, ''Etymology''</ref>.

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA}}
* {{homophones|pt|Tomar}}
* {{audio|pt|Pt tomar.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb}}

# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[take]] {{gloss|to get something into one’s possession or control}}
#: {{ux|pt|Fui ao banco '''tomar''' meu dinheiro.|I went to the bank to '''get''' my money.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive|military}} to [[take]]; to [[conquer]] {{gloss|to seize control of a location}}
##: {{ux|pt|Os cruzados '''tomaram''' Jerusalém.|The crusaders '''took''' Jerusalem.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[steal]] {{gloss|to take something illegally}}
##: {{ux|pt|O ladrão '''tomou''' todo o meu dinheiro.|The thief '''has taken''' all my money.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[take]]; to [[receive]] {{gloss|to be the victim of an interaction}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''Tomei''' um soco na cara.|'''I took''' a punch to the face.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive|applicable to some nouns}} to put into practice
#: {{ux|pt|'''tomar''' uma decisão|to make a decision}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''tomar''' medidas|to take measures}}
# {{indtr|pt|por|ditr=1}} to [[take for]]; to [[consider]]; to [[regard]] {{gloss|to have a certain opinion about someone or something}}
#: {{ux|pt|Eu '''tomei''' a Maria por corrupta.|I '''took''' Mary for a corrupt woman.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to take into the body
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[drink]] {{gloss|to ingest a liquid}}
##: {{ux|pt|Eu '''tomei''' suco.|I '''drank''' juice.}}
## {{lb|pt|intransitive|by extension}} to [[drink]] {{gloss|to consume alcoholic beverages, especially habitually}}
##: {{ux|pt|Ele '''toma''' muito, durante os finais de semana.|He '''drinks''' a lot on weekends.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[take]] {{gloss|to use a medicine}}
##: {{ux|pt|Esqueci de '''tomar''' meus antidepressivos.|I forgot to '''take''' my antidepressants.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[take]]; to [[experience]], [[undergo]]
#: {{ux|pt|'''tomar''' um banho|to take a shower}}

